messages.content:
# OUTLINE PIPELINE PHASE 02: SECTION ARCHITECTURE

Timeline Lock does not apply during outlining; you are planning, not writing a Scene Card.

Return ONLY a single JSON object. No markdown, no code fences, no commentary.
Use strict JSON (double quotes, no trailing commas).

Goal:
- Define chapter-internal mini-arcs before scene listing.
- Do NOT emit scenes in this phase.

Required output schema:
{
  "schema_version": "sections_v1",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "chapter_id": 1,
      "sections": [
        {
          "section_id": 1,
          "title": "",
          "intent": "",
          "section_role": "setup",
          "target_scene_count": 3,
          "end_condition": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Rules:
- Include every chapter_id from outline_spine_v1.
- section_id must be sequential integers within each chapter starting at 1.
- Typical section count per chapter is 3-8; interlude/transition chapters may use 2-4.
- target_scene_count should usually be 2-6.
- section intents must be distinct and progressive.
- end_condition is required and must define deterministic section closure target.
- The section-final scene in phase 03 must echo end_condition exactly via end_condition_echo.
- Keep chapter goals/bridges unchanged from phase 01.
- Sum of section target_scene_count should approximately align with chapter expected_scene_count.

If you cannot satisfy constraints after correction attempts, return error_v1:
{
  "result": "ERROR",
  "schema_version": "error_v1",
  "error_type": "validation_error",
  "reason_code": "section_architecture_incomplete",
  "missing_fields": ["chapters[0].sections[0].end_condition"],
  "phase": "phase_02_section_architecture",
  "action_hint": "Provide sequential section ids and non-empty end_condition for each section."
}

Outline spine (phase 01):
{
  "chapters": [
    {
      "bridge": {
        "from_prev": "Arlo's mundane life ends in a freak vending machine accident.",
        "to_next": "Arlo realizes he needs a way to monetize his 'Run' mechanic without getting killed by the first mob that touches him."
      },
      "chapter_id": 1,
      "chapter_role": "hook",
      "goal": "Protagonist Arlo is isekai'd into 'Aethelgard Online' and discovers that his 'Luck' stat is so low it has integer-overflowed into a guaranteed 'Crit Hit' on every strike, provided he is running away.",
      "pacing": {
        "expected_scene_count": 8,
        "intensity": 4,
        "tempo": "rush"
      },
      "stakes_shift": "From confused victim to accidental glass-cannon exploiter.",
      "title": "The 100% Critical Failure"
    },
    {
      "bridge": {
        "from_prev": "Arlo identifies the 'Coward's Strike' exploit.",
        "to_next": "The massive loot drop from the Guardian flags Arlo's account for 'unusual activity' in the local region."
      },
      "chapter_id": 2,
      "chapter_role": "setup",
      "goal": "Arlo must defeat the Tutorial Guardian using only retreat-based attacks to secure enough starting gold for a 'Dash' skill book.",
      "pacing": {
        "expected_scene_count": 10,
        "intensity": 3,
        "tempo": "steady"
      },
      "stakes_shift": "From penniless newbie to a player with a unique, albeit cowardly, combat style.",
      "title": "Kiting the Tutorial Boss"
    },
    {
      "bridge": {
        "from_prev": "Arlo enters the main hub with a bag full of 'impossible' loot.",
        "to_next": "To prove he isn't a hacker, Arlo is forced into a 'Trial of the Coward' by the local guild leader."
      },
      "chapter_id": 3,
      "chapter_role": "pressure",
      "goal": "Arlo attempts to sell his high-tier tutorial loot in the city of Oakhaven but is intercepted by a guild of 'Min-Maxers' who suspect him of hacking.",
      "pacing": {
        "expected_scene_count": 12,
        "intensity": 3,
        "tempo": "steady"
      },
      "stakes_shift": "From solo survival to navigating player-driven politics and accusations.",
      "title": "The Gilded Scoundrel's Guild"
    },
    {
      "bridge": {
        "from_prev": "The guild leader sets a 'no-frontal-damage' challenge.",
        "to_next": "The dungeon run uncovers a hidden 'System Glitch' zone that only Arlo can navigate."
      },
      "chapter_id": 4,
      "chapter_role": "trial",
      "goal": "Arlo must clear a low-level dungeon while never facing an enemy head-on to satisfy the guild's curiosity and earn their protection.",
      "pacing": {
        "expected_scene_count": 11,
        "intensity": 2,
        "tempo": "slow_burn"
      },
      "stakes_shift": "From being a social pariah to gaining a reluctant, confused ally in the guild's scout, Jax.",
      "title": "The Trial of the Yellow Streak"
    },
    {
      "bridge": {
        "from_prev": "The System detects the 'Luck' overflow and schedules a fix.",
        "to_next": "Arlo and Jax must race through a high-level territory to reach the 'Source Code' altar."
      },
      "chapter_id": 5,
      "chapter_role": "reversal",
      "goal": "A world-wide announcement declares an emergency maintenance patch to 'fix combat exploits'; Arlo must reach the Glitch Zone's heart to lock in his 'Coward' status as a permanent Title before the server resets.",
      "pacing": {
        "expected_scene_count": 12,
        "intensity": 5,
        "tempo": "rush"
      },
      "stakes_shift": "From a temporary exploit to a permanent, system-recognized class identity.",
      "title": "Patch Notes and Panic"
    },
    {
      "bridge": {
        "from_prev": "The Sentinel blocks the path to the Altar.",
        "to_next": "The Altar is activated as the world fades to white for the 'update'."
      },
      "chapter_id": 6,
      "chapter_role": "confrontation",
      "goal": "Arlo faces the Zone Sentinel\u2014a boss designed to punish runners\u2014and must use his 'Crit Hit & Run' style to survive long enough for the patch timer to expire.",
      "pacing": {
        "expected_scene_count": 14,
        "intensity": 5,
        "tempo": "rush"
      },
      "stakes_shift": "From being fixed/deleted to becoming a 'Legacy Bug'\u2014an unpatchable anomaly.",
      "title": "Running for His Life (Literally)"
    },
    {
      "bridge": {
        "from_prev": "The server comes back online with Arlo's stats intact.",
        "to_next": "The major guilds realize Arlo is the only one who can clear the new 'Endgame' content released in the patch."
      },
      "chapter_id": 7,
      "chapter_role": "aftermath",
      "goal": "Arlo wakes up post-patch to find he has been granted the unique Title 'The Unfixable One', making him the only player capable of damaging 'Invulnerable' admin-level mobs.",
      "pacing": {
        "expected_scene_count": 9,
        "intensity": 3,
        "tempo": "steady"
      },
      "stakes_shift": "From a lucky coward to the most valuable (and hunted) asset in the game.",
      "title": "The Legacy of the Glitch"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "spine_v1"
}

